      section
        h1 Libp2p and Peer-to-Peer Messaging
        p 
          | Libp2p is a modular network stack that allows developers to build peer-to-peer applications easily. 
          | It provides essential networking components such as transport protocols, stream multiplexing, 
          | encryption, and peer discovery, making it easy to create decentralized applications.
        p
          | With Libp2p, you can establish direct communication between peers without relying on a central server. 
          | This enables applications like messaging, file sharing, and real-time collaboration tools.
        p
          | To implement peer-to-peer messaging using Libp2p, you can set up a Libp2p node with modules like 
          | TCP for transport, Noise or Secio for encryption, and Mplex or Yamux for stream multiplexing. 
          | PubSub modules like FloodSub or Gossipsub can be used to manage message distribution across peers.